# Go
server/relayium-server
server/relayium
server/relayium.db
server/relayium.db-wal
server/relayium.db-shm
/dist/
# Node
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# auto-deploy runtime state (server-local, never committed)
/web/dist
/web/releases/
/.deployed-sha
server/relayium-node

# Compose reads a project-root .env for variable interpolation, so a self-hoster
# following docs/self-hosting.md may create one holding a real TURN secret.
# server/.gitignore already covers server/.env; the repository root did not.
/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example

# macOS
**/.DS_Store

# Superpowers workspace (planning docs, internal scratch)
.superpowers/

# Production ops (moved to the private relayium-ops repo; must never be
# re-committed here — nginx/coturn configs and the systemd unit are private)
/deploy/

# Local browser evidence and auxiliary worktrees are machine-scoped scratch,
# never product source. Named Playwright sessions may create the directory at
# either the repository root or a package working directory.
.playwright-cli/
.worktrees/
# Screenshots a named Playwright session writes for one investigation. Same
# category as the session directory above: evidence for a review, reproducible
# from the wrapper, and specific to the machine that captured it.
/output/
# The same evidence dropped at the repository ROOT instead — a screenshot pasted
# into a review or a bug report. Root-anchored on purpose: a product asset that
# happens to be named screenshot-*.png under web/ or apps/ is still tracked.
/screenshot-*.png
# Two-device iOS acceptance evidence: scripts/ios-device-pair-acceptance.sh and
# scripts/ios-device-inbox-acceptance.sh keep their run directory whatever the
# outcome, because a pass is evidence too. Each run leaves logs, .xcresult
# bundles and a DerivedData tree, so the roots reach multiple gigabytes. This is
# intentionally retained local physical evidence, not build scratch to clean.
# Root-anchored: only the evidence roots at the repository root are ignored.
/.relayium-device-inbox/
/.relayium-device-pair/
